  "claims": [
    "Settlements form an additive composition surface with identity, inverse, commutativity, and associativity facts over net token deltas.",
    "Balanced settlements are exactly zero net-flow settlements and are closed under settlement composition.",
    "CPMM swap, LP deposit, LP withdrawal, and roundtrip settlement helpers preserve the declared net-flow and safety relationships under their stated bounds.",
    "Batch settlement conversion composes homomorphically, safe batches imply safe settlement, and batch CPMM execution preserves monotone K-growth in the modeled CPMM state.",
    "Canonical execution certificates enforce volume maximality, surplus maximality among volume ties, and order minimality among objective ties.",
    "Mechanism obligations imply canonical safe settlement when generator coverage, winner certification, feasibility, and trace realization all hold."
  ],
  "proof_method": [
    "additive group and homomorphism algebra over integer settlement deltas",
